## Rollout, gating, and observability

The rollout should be phased so that you do not turn the governance layer into the new source of friction. Start by adding observability and non-blocking contract checks, then add blocking `agentStop` enforcement, then add local Sonar fast-path checks, and only after that make CI governance and quality gates required branch checks. GitHub’s custom-agent testing guidance explicitly recommends testing custom agents privately before release, and GitHub’s protected-branch documentation supports required checks before merging. citeturn36view3turn36view4turn7view1

